Create a 12-minute video lecture. Begin with an engaging animated sequence illustrating a benevolent AI agent transforming into one with unintended biases. Explain beneficence, non-maleficence, fairness, transparency, and accountability using relatable analogies (e.g., a self-driving car for non-maleficence, a loan application agent for fairness). Include side-by-side text overlays defining key terms. Discuss common pitfalls like data bias and the "black box" problem. Use a simple AutoGen code snippet demonstrating how an agent's prompt can inadvertently introduce bias (e.g., "prioritize speed over equity"). Conclude with a reflection prompt asking learners to consider an ethical dilemma in their own domain. Ensure high-contrast visuals and captions for accessibility.

